DexSwapModule::validate
├── when params are too short
│   └── it should return false with invalid params encoding
├── when target token is zero address
│   └── it should return false with zero target token
├── when target token equals sell token
│   └── it should return false with same input and output token
├── when amount is zero
│   └── it should return false with zero sell amount
├── when maxSlippageBps is zero or exceeds 10000
│   └── it should return false with invalid slippage bps
├── when sell token price feed is zero address
│   └── it should return false with missing sell token price feed
├── when buy token price feed is zero address
│   └── it should return false with missing buy token price feed
├── when max staleness is zero
│   └── it should return false with zero max staleness
├── when swap deadline seconds is zero
│   └── it should return false with zero swap deadline
├── when oracle price is unavailable
│   └── it should return false with oracle price unavailable
├── when caller has insufficient balance
│   └── it should return false with insufficient balance
├── when amount exceeds maxAmount
│   └── it should return false with exceeds max swap amount
├── when amount equals or is below maxAmount
│   └── it should return true
├── when maxAmount is zero
│   └── it should impose no limit and return true
├── when all validations pass
│   └── it should return true with empty reason
├── validate and execute should agree on failure reasons (shared _validate)
│   ├── it should agree on params too short
│   ├── it should agree on zero target token
│   ├── it should agree on zero sell amount
│   ├── it should agree on same input and output token
│   ├── it should agree when both oracle and balance are bad
│   └── it should agree on exceeds max swap amount
└── fuzz: validate and execute agreement
    └── it should produce identical failure reasons for shared validation checks
